#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054368 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054643 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "49ab93ca-16ca-5e57-835f-036b59f25d63" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Truth Values of Compound Statements"}] :question/id #uuid "6497cb54-2453-5dd7-8b97-09e06280d774" :question/math-academy-id "e-12693" :question/problem "Consider the following compound statement:\n\n$$\n\\underbrace{5 \\vphantom{p}\\textrm{ is prime} }_A \\quad \\underbrace{\\vphantom{p}\\textbf{or}}_{\\lor} \\quad \\underbrace{\\dfrac13 \\in \\mathbb{Z}}_B\n$$\n\nFind the truth values of the statements $A$ and $B,$ and the compound statement $A\\lor B.$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the following facts about the \"and\" $(\\land)$ and \"or\" $(\\lor)$ logical connectives:\n\n- The statement $A \\land B$ is true if *both* $A$ and $B$ are true.\n\n- The statement $A \\lor B$ is true if either $A$ is true, or $B$ is true, or *both* $A$ and $B$ are true.\n\nIn our case, $A$ is true, and $B$ is false. Therefore, the result is true:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\underbrace{5\\text{ is prime}}_{A}\\,\\underbrace{\\text{or}}_{∨}\\,\\underbrace{\\frac{1}{3}\\in Z}_{B} & \\,\\,≡\\,\\text{true}∨\\text{false}≡\\text{true}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054389 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054644 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2c15e521-f848-5d9c-ba06-00550277b8cb" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Truth Values of Complex Statements"}] :question/id #uuid "9209c4e5-30e0-5933-9c41-32750b5301ad" :question/math-academy-id "e-12895" :question/problem "Consider the following compound statement:\n\n$$\n\\underbrace{\\mathbb{Z}\\cup \\mathbb{R}=\\mathbb{Z} }_P \n\\quad \\underbrace{\\vphantom{|}\\textbf{and}}_{\\land} \\quad \\underbrace{\\overbrace{7 \\,|\\, 21}^Q \n\\quad \\overbrace{\\vphantom{|}\\textbf{or}}^{\\lor} \\quad \n\\overbrace{7 \\,|\\, 29}^R }_{Q \\, \\lor \\, R}\n$$\n\nFind the truth values of the statements $P,$ $Q$ and $R,$ and the compound statements $Q\\lor R$ and $P\\land (Q\\lor R).$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the following facts about the \"and\" $(\\land)$ and \"or\" $(\\lor)$ logical connectives:\n\n- The statement $A \\land B$ is true if *both* $A$ and $B$ are true.\n\n- The statement $A \\lor B$ is true if either $A$ is true, or $B$ is true, or *both* $A$ and $B$ are true.\n\nIn our case, $P$ is false, $Q$ is true, and $R$ is false. Therefore, $Q \\lor R$ is true, but the result is false:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P∧(Q∨R) & ≡\\text{false}∧\\overbrace{(\\text{true}∨\\text{false})}^{\\text{true}} \\\\  & ≡\\text{false}∧\\text{true} \\\\  & ≡\\text{false}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054396 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054606 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fdadd355-0ce5-598a-b9cd-f189ccfb7ca6" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating Expressions With Stand-Alone Exponents"}] :question/id #uuid "6ce1d2ce-e99a-5f5c-a698-3f744805ef24" :question/math-academy-id "e-12921" :question/problem "Calculate $(-3)^3 \\div 6$." :question/worked-solution "To evaluate this expression, we use PEMDAS. First, we compute the exponents:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\underbrace{(-3)^{3}}_{-27}÷6=(-27)÷6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we divide:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-27)÷6 & = \\\\ \\frac{(-27)}{6} & = \\\\ -\\frac{27}{6} & = \\\\ -\\frac{27÷3}{6÷3} & = \\\\ -\\frac{9}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054397 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054607 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cd0c74c4-8496-5bfa-add1-5c3fed61d13f" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating Expressions With Exponents Outside Parentheses"}] :question/id #uuid "d4bc50be-7125-55ef-9d29-c69af56e25d3" :question/math-academy-id "e-12922" :question/problem "Evaluate $(1-4)^2 \\times \\dfrac{1}{12}.$" :question/worked-solution "To evaluate this expression, we use PEMDAS. First, we perform the operation inside the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\underbrace{1-4}_{-3})^{2}\\times \\frac{1}{12} & =(-3)^{2}\\times \\frac{1}{12}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we compute the exponents:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\underbrace{(-3)^{2}}_{9}\\times \\frac{1}{12} & =9\\times \\frac{1}{12}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we multiply:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9\\times \\frac{1}{12} & = \\\\ \\frac{9}{1}\\times \\frac{1}{12} & = \\\\ \\frac{9\\times 1}{1\\times 12} & = \\\\ \\frac{9}{12} & = \\\\ \\frac{9÷3}{12÷3} & = \\\\ \\frac{3}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054398 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054608 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4cc66e18-1adb-5bec-a6c6-f434ebf4ed13" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating Expressions With Exponents Inside Parentheses"}] :question/id #uuid "21fccd11-6107-53b8-beb0-d0c39f23bc17" :question/math-academy-id "e-12923" :question/problem "What is the value of $\\left( 5 \\div (-2)^2 \\right) \\times \\left( -\\dfrac{4}{5} \\right).$" :question/worked-solution "To evaluate this expression, we use PEMDAS. First, consider the expression inside the parenthesis:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5÷(-2)^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying PEMDAS to this expression, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5÷(-2)^{2} & = \\\\ 5÷4 & = \\\\ \\frac{5}{4} & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we multiply:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\overbrace{5÷(-2)^{2}}^{\\frac{5}{4}})\\times (-\\frac{4}{5}) & = \\\\ \\frac{5}{4}\\times (-\\frac{4}{5}) & = \\\\ -\\frac{5}{4}\\times \\frac{4}{5} & = \\\\ -\\frac{5\\times 4}{4\\times 5} & = \\\\ -\\frac{\\cancel{5}\\times \\cancel{4}}{\\cancel{4}\\times \\cancel{5}} & = \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186055037 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054642 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5e2ea816-3a62-5167-9f08-17ebcf97c22e" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing Nested Compound Statements in Symbolic Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cc55069c-667c-5e08-b2b0-341a1b91bc8e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R∨(S∨T)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186051753} {:answer/id #uuid "d4920408-8a32-5926-8964-f320c3ee7ae1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R∨(S∧T)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186051754} {:answer/id #uuid "d8af7fc3-5f6b-5139-9b22-d82aba7b2766" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(R∨S)∨T" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186051755} {:answer/id #uuid "e1eff23a-ece4-5063-9fd2-b91ca4789a60" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R∧(S∧T)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186051756} {:answer/id #uuid "e6d624ca-e16c-5795-906f-04ab06d6cdab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(R∧S)∨T" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186051757}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d4920408-8a32-5926-8964-f320c3ee7ae1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R∨(S∧T)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186051754} :answer-field/id #uuid "b4759e44-79a1-5658-a783-9ae9824ce60b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186051752}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c3a7db47-e883-5a71-8bfd-ec843bd98b41" :question/math-academy-id "q-170852" :question/problem "$2$ is prime, **or** $14$ is a multiple of $7$ **and** $5.$\n\nExpress the compound statement above in symbolic form given the following notations:\n\n- $R:2\\text{ is prime}$\n\n- $S:14\\text{ is a multiple of }7$\n\n- $T:14\\text{ is a multiple of }5$" :question/worked-solution "The word \"and\" is represented by the symbol \"$∧$\", while the word \"or\" is represented by the symbol \"$∨$\".\n\nNote that this sentence consists of two parts:\n\n- **Part 1:** $2$ is prime. This corresponds to $R.$\n\n- **Part 2:** $14$ is a multiple of $7$ and $5.$ This corresponds to\n\n$$\n\\underbrace{14\\text{ is a multiple of }7}_{S}\\,\\underbrace{\\text{and}}_{∧}\\,\\underbrace{14\\text{ is a multiple of }5}_{T},\n$$\n\nthat is, $S∧T.$\n\nSo, we can express the sentence as\n\n$$\n\\underbrace{2\\text{ is prime}}_{R}\\,\\underbrace{\\text{or}}_{∨}\\,\\underbrace{14\\text{ is a multiple of }7\\text{ and }5}_{S\\,∧\\,T},\n$$\n\nthat is, $R∨(S∧T).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186055038 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054642 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5e2ea816-3a62-5167-9f08-17ebcf97c22e" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing Nested Compound Statements in Symbolic Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8a1a320b-966c-5be5-b55c-cbf763e21be4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(P∨D)∨(Q∨L)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186051759} {:answer/id #uuid "4283cb0a-bc15-539e-bf50-135ce5033b34" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "((P∨D)∧Q)∨L" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186051760} {:answer/id #uuid "4b7b3a4d-47d3-594a-8f79-facb724ae543" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(P∨D)∧(Q∨L)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186051761} {:answer/id #uuid "5afc11cd-8133-54ba-abc7-7da1178c534e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(P∧D)∧(Q∧L)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186051762} {:answer/id #uuid "7d3b904f-54f4-52dd-ae8a-33ab17b5e174" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "((P∧D)∧Q)∧L" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186051763}] :answer-field/id #uuid "f6e98999-2f83-5c15-8552-57096b430901" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186051758} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5049d692-27fe-5178-b0cc-6e568a7e059e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(P∨D)∧(Q∨L)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378977} {:answer/id #uuid "5adfd8ff-c3d0-5d07-a448-db44835fa4f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(P∨D)∨(Q∨L)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378978} {:answer/id #uuid "95831cd8-8683-5b4f-aa8c-27abdaf6bf80" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(P∧D)∧(Q∧L)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378979} {:answer/id #uuid "8552798a-bfd1-5074-b508-9246eaf75b0a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "((P∨D)∧Q)∨L" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378980} {:answer/id #uuid "9f092933-9419-5b92-8adf-d93b7d16f997" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "((P∧D)∧Q)∧L" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378981}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5049d692-27fe-5178-b0cc-6e568a7e059e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(P∨D)∧(Q∨L)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378977} :answer-field/id #uuid "421304ea-9da1-51d7-80ea-0a45c6a0bab2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378976}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "adc8afd5-e27f-547d-aa56-e27aaed8127d" :question/math-academy-id "q-170853" :question/problem "$7$ is prime **or** divisible by $10,$ **and** $5$ is rational **or** less than $100.$\n\nExpress the compound statement above in symbolic form given the following notations:\n\n- $P:7\\text{ is prime}$\n\n- $D:7\\text{ is divisible by }10$\n\n- $Q:5\\text{ is rational}$\n\n- $L:5\\text{ is less than }100$" :question/worked-solution "The word \"and\" is represented by the symbol \"$∧$\", while the word \"or\" is represented by the symbol \"$∨$\".\n\nNote that this sentence consists of two parts:\n\n- **Part 1:** $7$ is prime or divisible by $10.$ This corresponds to\n\n$$\n\\underbrace{7\\text{ is prime}}_{P}\\,\\underbrace{\\text{or}}_{∨}\\,\\underbrace{7\\text{ is divisible by }10}_{D}\n$$\n\nthat is, $P∨D.$\n\n- **Part 2:** $5$ is rational or less than $100.$ This corresponds to\n\n$$\n\\underbrace{5\\text{ is rational}}_{Q}\\,\\underbrace{\\text{or}}_{∨}\\,\\underbrace{5\\text{ is less than }100}_{L},\n$$\n\nthat is, $Q∨L.$\n\nSo, we can express the sentence as\n\n$$\n\\underbrace{7\\text{ is prime }\\text{or}\\text{ divisible by }10}_{P\\,∨\\,D}\\,\\underbrace{\\text{and}}_{∧}\\,\\underbrace{5\\text{ is rational }\\text{or}\\text{ less than }100}_{Q\\,∨\\,L},\n$$\n\nthat is, $(P∨D)∧(Q∨L).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186055061 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054644 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2c15e521-f848-5d9c-ba06-00550277b8cb" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Truth Values of Complex Statements"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "89ac148b-88b6-5bc6-a50e-f6603a28bd8e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186051860} {:answer/id #uuid "c9897358-adb8-5e1a-abf0-2d661694ad76" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186051861}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "89ac148b-88b6-5bc6-a50e-f6603a28bd8e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186051860} :answer-field/id #uuid "9536c9e0-ac5b-5ad6-967b-f24ae2574aec" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186051859} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "91e5774d-2cce-564e-93fc-f483e9cd65d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186051863} {:answer/id #uuid "10719c54-1dab-5966-88d9-a1bf063cc3d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186051864}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "91e5774d-2cce-564e-93fc-f483e9cd65d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186051863} :answer-field/id #uuid "0bb9d202-9d4e-572a-b68b-0edba4a190bc" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186051862} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "da4a1be6-a1e9-5d40-b946-7c37e2eb3033" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186051866} {:answer/id #uuid "ed99a2e9-9e65-5722-b045-05d6294b9253" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186051867}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ed99a2e9-9e65-5722-b045-05d6294b9253" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186051867} :answer-field/id #uuid "f989fd77-3e92-59ca-858d-56bb61a0b369" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186051865}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6b084eee-0807-5bb1-bc2e-918712bbc035" :question/math-academy-id "q-178152" :question/problem "$$\n\\underbrace{\\overbrace{{3}^{2}=9}^{P}\\,\\overbrace{\\text{and}}^{∧}\\,\\overbrace{2\\text{ is rational}}^{Q}}_{P\\,∧\\,Q}\\,\\underbrace{\\text{and}}_{∧}\\,\\underbrace{\\sqrt{5}\\text{ is irrational}}_{R}\n$$\n\nFor the compound statement above, we have that\n\n$\\,$ $P∧Q$ is {{field-1}},\n$\\,$ $R$ is {{field-2}},\n$\\,$ $(P∧Q)∧R$ is {{field-3}}." :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the following facts about the \"and\" $(∧)$ and \"or\" $(∨)$ logical connectives:\n\n- The statement $A∧B$ is true if *both* $A$ and $B$ are true.\n\n- The statement $A∨B$ is true if either $A$ is true, or $B$ is true, or *both* $A$ and $B$ are true.\n\nIn our case, $P$ is true, $Q$ is true, and $R$ is true. Therefore, $P∧Q$ is true, and the result is true:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(P∧Q)∧R & ≡\\overbrace{(\\text{true}∧\\text{true})}^{\\text{true}}∧\\text{true} \\\\  & ≡\\text{true}∧\\text{true} \\\\  & ≡\\text{true}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186055087 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054643 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "49ab93ca-16ca-5e57-835f-036b59f25d63" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Truth Values of Compound Statements"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9f4e9e86-8284-5124-a5d8-2986c678430f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186051966} {:answer/id #uuid "351e3b6e-328b-51b3-a3b4-654ed5082185" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186051967}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "351e3b6e-328b-51b3-a3b4-654ed5082185" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186051967} :answer-field/id #uuid "5f130160-11dc-5d3a-9856-5fbf9e017de3" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186051965} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a784ae67-278a-5990-a46b-9305f5e46ed4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186051969} {:answer/id #uuid "ec33348b-a0de-5fdb-82f8-56f288950968" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186051970}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a784ae67-278a-5990-a46b-9305f5e46ed4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186051969} :answer-field/id #uuid "80f5e149-319b-5aca-8113-65c296ae9284" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186051968} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0974b375-a54a-5d5e-846e-11f8487271d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186051972} {:answer/id #uuid "40bf36f3-987d-514b-a937-3a85bd10e5c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186051973}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "40bf36f3-987d-514b-a937-3a85bd10e5c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186051973} :answer-field/id #uuid "cbf02d32-be98-53f4-bb26-71699b829f9f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186051971}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "251d1784-5e7a-5d2b-9609-81be8de6d435" :question/math-academy-id "q-181713" :question/problem "$$\n\\underbrace{2\\text{ is negative}}_{A}\\,\\underbrace{\\text{or}}_{∨}\\,\\underbrace{0.5\\text{ is rational}}_{B}\n$$\n\nFor the compound statement above, we have that\n\n$\\,$ $A$ is {{field-1}},\n$\\,$ $B$ is {{field-2}},\n$\\,$ $A∨B$ is {{field-3}}." :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the following facts about the \"and\" $(∧)$ and \"or\" $(∨)$ logical connectives:\n\n- The statement $A∧B$ is true if *both* $A$ and $B$ are true.\n\n- The statement $A∨B$ is true if either $A$ is true, or $B$ is true, or *both* $A$ and $B$ are true.\n\nIn our case, $A$ is false, and $B$ is true. Therefore, the result is true:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\underbrace{2\\text{ is negative}}_{A}\\,\\underbrace{\\text{or}}_{∨}\\,\\underbrace{0.5\\text{ is rational}}_{B} & \\,\\,≡\\,\\text{false}∨\\text{true}≡\\text{true}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186055088 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054644 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2c15e521-f848-5d9c-ba06-00550277b8cb" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Truth Values of Complex Statements"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8b50b7d4-3c3b-5d98-a292-8fa5da2eb9e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186051975} {:answer/id #uuid "eb41b5c2-1133-50fc-a410-f61a02f97531" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186051976}] :answer-field/id #uuid "c3340bc4-717b-59f4-9e36-ecb14332f040" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186051974} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "02d5be3d-6e6e-555b-a76b-e2b5c89d8c8d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186051978} {:answer/id #uuid "1cf6e2bb-e24a-5dd7-aae6-d0039d0ee2a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186051979}] :answer-field/id #uuid "9a919079-b616-5ba6-95d6-72c772ea2105" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186051977} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7ec56ef9-9470-5dd9-aa39-b227d829c786" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379105} {:answer/id #uuid "e444d8d9-bc1a-530